.TH AVR\-VM\-FORK 1 "" "avr 0.5.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-fork \- Boot a copy of a PAUSED VM's disk; the source remains paused.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm fork
[OPTIONS] VM_ID_OR_NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Boot a copy of a PAUSED VM's disk; the source remains paused.
.PP
Copies the source's machine configuration and disk, including its SSH host keys and password, but discards memory state. A scoped-token password may be replaced without returning its replacement. No password is returned; use update --rotate-password if needed. Requires admin access to the source.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fITEXT\fR
Fork name. Defaults to a name derived from the source.
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fITEXT\fR
Fork TTL (e.g. 8h, 7d). Default 8h, max 7d.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait for the fork to become connectable.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
(default: 300)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the fork VM as JSON.
